  "body_html": "<h1>Self-Dual Lattice Function</h1>\n<p>Let \\(V\\) carry a nondegenerate sesquilinear form. For an \\(o_D\\)-lattice \\(L\\subseteq V\\), its dual is\n\\[\nL^\\vee=\\{v\\in V : \\langle v,L\\rangle_V\\subseteq \\mathbf p_D\\}.\n\\]</p>\n<p>For a lattice function \\(L\\), the dual lattice function is defined by\n\\[\n(L^\\vee)_s=(L_{(-s)+})^\\vee.\n\\]\nThe lattice function is self-dual when \\(L=L^\\vee\\). Under the Bruhat-Tits identification for classical groups, points in the building correspond to self-dual lattice functions.</p>",
  "proof_html": null,
